.TH TLS_SERVERNAME 3
.SH NAME
tls_servername \- set the server name a TLS client announces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <tls.h>
.P
.BI "int tls_servername(fd_type " fd ", const char* " name ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tls_servername ()
sets the server name indication (SNI) of the TLS instance of
.I fd
to
.IR name .
It has to be called after
.BR tls_client (3)
and before
.BR tls_connect (3).
Servers that host many names, as the big API providers do, select the
certificate and often accept the connection only with it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 on success, 0 if
.I fd
has no TLS instance or the name was refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
tls_connect(3)
